From dddab5a25f65e58f991c146618ca4135e8c81a6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iamwrm <iamwrm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:52:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] feat(client): mirror the terminal-ansi frame stream in
 a screen model

Predictive local echo (i0002 W3) needs the terminal-ansi client to know
what is on screen: cursor position, cell contents, and whether a cell is
unstyled. New src/client/screen_model.rs replays received TerminalFrame
bytes into a cell grid.

The frame stream comes exclusively from BlitEncoder, whose vocabulary is
small and has no scrolling or relative cursor motion. Cell runs begin at
an absolute CUP, but adjacent cells can continue inline. Split printable
runs at Unicode extended grapheme boundaries so ASCII-leading decomposed
clusters remain one modeled cell. The parser also covers SGR (tracking
only plain-vs-styled pen), 2J, ?25h/l, ?2026 sync, DECSCUSR, OSC 8
hyperlinks, OSC 52, and Kitty APC passthrough. apply() reports touched
cells for prediction reconciliation.

Round-trip tests validate the model against real BlitEncoder full and diff
output, including contiguous ASCII, ASCII-prefix decomposed graphemes,
wide chars, hyperlinks, and hidden cursors. Not wired into the client loop
yet; the prediction engine lands separately.
